          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most cracked concrete patios need filling, not replacing. If the slab is flat and solid, clean the cracks, seal them with a flexible product and resurface only if the surface itself is worn.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Offset, rocking or crumbling slabs are a different problem. Level the sunken sections, cover a stable but ugly slab, or replace the parts that have failed, and fix the drainage that caused it either way.
          </p>
